CORE wide-pointer-encoding no-new-smt broken-smt-backend
main.c
--wide-pointer-encoding --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* reachable: assumed address reuse not over-constrained: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With wide pointer encoding, __CPROVER_assume(p == q) between two dynamic
objects whose addresses may be reused after free must remain satisfiable: the
full-bitvector identity forced for assumed pointer equalities
(boolbv_set_equality_to_true) must not over-constrain the model to UNSAT, so
the assertion is reachable.
